description:
A ring-fit benchmark that any ring fit is scored against, split out of CRAW-106 so the follow-on clustering fit (CRAW-112) can build on master without CRAW-106's fit, which may not land.

From CRAW-106 it takes only:
- the 17 ring_fit_* fixtures (pinched tori and a horned sphere with rings and bisectors drawn off the grooves), with the trailing fit_ring_anchors node dropped, so each fixture ends on the rings as drawn;
- RingAnchorFitTest's expectations (where each ring should end, in degrees round the torus or round the tube, or on the horn's foot circle, and the tolerances), turned into a harness that takes any fit and reports how far each ring's anchors end from where they should;
- CRAW-106's scores on it, as the baseline to beat, measured in the craw-106 worktree and recorded on this ticket.

Not taken: RingAnchorFit, FitRingAnchorsNode, SurfaceHeatDistance, AnchorGrooveFit, RingBlend, AnchoredRings, the ring scene and tool changes.
